      "text": [
        "5838 - وَ قَالَ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ : \"خَمْسٌ هُنَّ كَمَا أَقُولُ لَيْسَتْ لِبَخِيلٍ رَاحَةٌ وَ لاَ لِحَسُودٍ لَذَّةٌ وَ لاَ لِلْمَمْلُوكِ وَفَاءٌ وَ لاَ لِكَذُوبٍ مُرُوءَةٌ وَ لاَ يَسُودُ سَفِيهٌ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.5838 - Abu Abdullah Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq (as) said:\n\"Five things are exactly as I say:\nA miser will never find comfort,\nA jealous person will never experience pleasure,\nA slave will not have loyalty,\nA liar will have no honor,\nAnd a foolish person will never attain leadership.\""
        ]
      }
